{
  "heading": "Idaho Climate Conversations",
  "eyebrow": "Summer 2023 · All 44 counties",
  "lede": "Two friends, one Prius, and a simple question for every Idaho county: what changes have you seen?",
  "body": "In June 2023, my friend Jane Carney and I drove a Prius through all 44 Idaho counties and sat down with about three people in each one, including at least one person under 18. We asked how the climate had changed where they live and how it touches their families and communities. We didn’t argue. We listened.\n\nThe result is over 100 short conversations with Idahoans of all ages, from the Panhandle to the Snake River Plain. Some people are alarmed, some are skeptical, and many simply describe what they have seen: the snowpack, the smoke, the water. The project was funded by a community GoFundMe and my mentor: Dr. Aly Bean.",
